WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.910
See? We just make each other better.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:10.720
Hello.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.950
You are all out of orange juice.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:13.780
I understand.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.670
I have to go out for orange juice.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.470
Yes, I understand.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.840
I have to go out for orange juice.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.620
Mitchell, I have to go out for orange juice.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.020
I have a problem with Russians.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.850
Being married to a Pritchett is great.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:31.630
So great.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.440
The best.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.930
But they can be a tad judgmental.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:35.740
Almost punitive.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.910
They are monsters.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.130
That's why the three of us formed a secret

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.200
alliance to help each other cover up our-

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.250
our little mistakes.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.750
Like back in December when I hastily

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.490
purchased an expensive prop for an open

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:48.300
house. Thanks so much for hiding it.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.320
Claire would kill me.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.000
And it's only till Monday when I can return

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.090
it.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.690
Don't worry.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.270
Hide! Hide!

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.360
Hi. Oh.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.400
Welcome home.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.200
You're so early, right?

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.010
Not really.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.130
There is that smile that I love.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.810
Why don't you take me to lunch?

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.460
Okay. What happened here anyway?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.710
You get into Joe's scented markers again?

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.700
So now I have scary Russian squatters who

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.490
won't leave. We'll have a small window when

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:20.960
Mitchell goes to the gym. He usually

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.610
stretches, takes a lap around the locker

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:23.660
room, and then gets a smoothie.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.430
You to deal with the Russians, and I'll keep

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.870
Mitch distracted. Anything else?

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:27.620
Yes.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.930
Our gate is broken, and Stella keeps getting

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:32.180
out in the street. I bought her a shock

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:32.660
collar.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.070
We thought about getting one when Luke was

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.720
younger. Claire ended up just shaking a can

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.530
of pennies at him.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.180
It spooked her and she's hiding.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.310
We need to find her before Jay doesn't see

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.740
the collar. He has warned me many times not

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.360
to get one because they are cruel.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.010
All right, we'll deal with the Russians first

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.840
and come find Stella before the big vote.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.040
We do not have much time.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:49.700
We need to go.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.640
I actually ordered a sandwich.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.070
What are you doing here?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.160
Oh, I just came through the unsecured back

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.920
door. Hello again.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:02.370
Hi.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.080
We're still interested in your house.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.210
We just might be leaning towards this one.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.890
Oh, I'm very surprised.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.680
People that like cooking so much.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.390
Are you guys going to be happy with this

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.560
tiny little pantry that leads to a gigantic

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.280
pantry?

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.170
Are you ready to see the interactive nursery?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.730
Oh, the baby just kicked.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.020
Hey, are you all about to be my new neighbor?

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.400
Hope you like to party.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.920
My name's Fred. They call me peeper because,

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.510
well, that doesn't matter.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.160
Oh, yeah. Look at the chocolate chip

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.570
cookies. Kids, get in here.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.220
Get yourselves some supper.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.010
These are my blessings.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.630
Do I like ethnic women?

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.780
Guilty. Do you like farm-fresh eggs?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.950
I sold my very first house and destroyed my

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:47.910
swooper. Of course, the

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.160
only way you can destroy a real swooper is to

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.290
stab its reflection during the harvest moon.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.630
All right. We shouldn't be panicking, right?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.380
No, of course not. There's got to be a

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.630
million ways out of here.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.340
There's a security camera.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:02:59.760
Oh.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.670
Oh, no, no, no, it's old and broke.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.180
Help! Help!

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.040
We're stuck in here!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.000
Gloria, that didn't work five minutes ago and

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.890
it didn't work ten minutes ago.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.540
Why can't they hear me?

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.850
This vent has to go somewhere.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.210
Gloria Maria Ramirez Delgado Pritchett, you

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.350
are a genius.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.700
I know. Give me a boost.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.900
No, it should be me. You're right.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.980
Gloria, give cam a boost.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.430
No, I mean,

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.260
I should give you a boost.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.490
The process works.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.900
Why don't we use that trunk?

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.680
See, we just make each other better.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.700
Chair. Chair, who needs Pritchetts?

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.340
I'll steady it. Thank you again.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.690
Yeah. Okay.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.890
Okay, great.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:39.820
You're great.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:40.690
Oh.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.250
Great. Oh, God.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:43.570
All right.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.790
Let's Die-Hard this puppy.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.910
Oh, that's my shoulder.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.220
All right. Okay, in we go.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.200
All right. Now, Phil, every couple feet

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.270
knock so we know where you are.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:55.810
Got it.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.240
Okay, guys, I think I see an opening.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.350
We're saved.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.510
Yipee-Ki-Yay Mother-- Oh dear God.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.980
Phil. Phil. Phil.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.930
Good news guys, I see two people.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.730
Maybe I can get it. Oh, it's you.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.770
I'm gonna be the belle of the ball in this

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.960
dress. Stealing this award has given me the

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.930
confidence to crush everyone in my path.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.870
Permiso.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.660
I never even saw Gloria go into the dressing

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.700
room. But there she was, like a superhero,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.610
able to destroy confidence in a single pose.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.900
I'm glad I didn't go with the first dress.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.820
They'll take one look at this one and make

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:32.930
me principal.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.740
Oh, come on!

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.070
You know what? Maybe you should try the dress

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.480
on that lady's wearing.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.140
Oh my God, that was brilliant and humbling.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.180
You know, I pride myself on solving people

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.350
problems. You know what?

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.850
You still have the swooper. Maybe I could-

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.690
No, thanks.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.530
She just can't accept help, but I can.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.120
I'm thinking about rocking this for my date

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.620
with Brenda. Ignore the buttons.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.090
Can you tell this is a woman's coat?

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:57.930
Yes.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:04:59.190
There's nothing I can do.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.750
I can't go for that.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:01.620
No can do.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.630
Cameron here bought an eggshell drier.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.940
Not white, not oatmeal, not Swiss coffee.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.410
Not baby powder. Not bone.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.930
Eggshell. Look, Rob, is it?

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.100
That's interesting.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.840
Here's how this is going down.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.270
We don't leave without that eggshell drier.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.520
Not swan feather, not Chester pig white.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:17.820
I think we've

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:18.840
Covered the colors.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.410
I sell houses to people every day who ask me

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.790
where they should buy their dryer.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.710
I don't think you want me giving them any

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.030
static.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.270
I may have one in the back, but it takes two

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.380
guys to load the truck.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.970
And it's just me today.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:32.690
Is it?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.880
It was right about then that a question

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.620
started nagging at me.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.860
Is Phil sexy?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.590
There she is. Stella!

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.250
Hi. Thank God you found my dog.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.210
Thank you.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.130
This is my dog. Her name's Pinkie.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.870
No it's not. Her name is Stella.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.460
It says right here on the tag.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.210
Look.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.440
Uh. Excuse me.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.030
Hi, sweetie. What's your name?

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.920
Blanche. Shut up.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.000
Mitchell would die.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.350
Listen, we don't know you.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.000
You seem like a very sweet little girl.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.620
And right now, we're forced to.

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.810
I can't believe I'm saying this to you.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.270
Rely on the kindness of strangers.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.310
I'll sell it to you for $200.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:26.790
That's it.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.050
Give me my dog.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.840
Ahhh! Oh, really? The little girl thinks

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:31.890
because she can scream.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.150
She can get away with everything?

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:33.900
I can scream too.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.920
Ah!

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.360
Ah! Ah! Ahhhh!

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.190
What the hell sound is that?

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.230
Who knows how long this has been going on,

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.030
okay? They've been in cahoots, covering up

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:49.920
each other's mistakes before we've even had

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.330
a chance to shame them.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.030
Since this little alliance made a decision to

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.650
go behind our backs. Maybe we should make a

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.000
decision without them.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.430
Oh. Like where we're going on vacation?

00:06:59.430 --> 00:06:59.880
No.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.520
No, no, I like it, I like it.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.930
Let's do this. Let's go vote.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:04.650
Yep.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:06.720
Yep. You got it.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.640
Okay, we've reached a decision.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:12.930
Drum roll please. Close enough.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.780
The family is going to...

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.570
Italy!

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.390
Awwww, no.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.900
The cutest part is that they think it was

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.710
their idea.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.740
What are you making?

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.380
I'm making an Italian dish that Jay's mother

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.790
used to make.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:40.230
Breakfast

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.510
lasagna. Great call, Honey.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.600
Oh. Hey, sweetie.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:49.980
Your breakfast is on the table.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:50.850
What's this?

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.430
Oh. I've named him.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.190
It's Giovanni.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.920
I'm still thinking about that movie last

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:56.400
night.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.690
You picked a good one.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.820
Only the Italians could make something that

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:00.660
romantic.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.400
Flapjacks for me amore.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:08.550
Oh, grazie.

